  (wire (pts (xy 337.82 160.02) (xy 337.82 157.48))
    (stroke (width 0) (type default))
    (uuid 9d3390ff-fc1e-5a5b-9fa7-8f2523e63c92)
  )
  (text "CONTROLLER: Pimoroni Pico Plus 2 (RP2350, 16 MB flash, 8 MB PSRAM, USB-C). It has parts underneath, so it plugs into two 20-pin sockets.\nIts USB-C port is the player's only power and data connector: put it on the rear edge of the board.\nPin plan (from docs/DESIGN.md 5.4)\n  GP0-GP7  YM2612 data D0-D7 (PIO, must stay in order)    GP8, GP9  A0, A1    GP10 /WR    GP11 /IC (reset)\n  GP21     7.67 MHz chip clock (GPOUT0: 153.33 MHz / 20)\n  GP14, GP15  I2C1 SDA / SCL to the LCD (through the level shifter on the Front panel page)\n  GP16 Play  GP17 Stop  GP18 Left  GP19 Right  GP20 Edit  GP22 Exit  GP26 Write   (buttons to GND, internal pull-ups)\n  GP27, GP28  data knob A / B\n  GP12     headphone amp enable (high = on), also on J1    GP13  spare, on J1 (not fitted)\n/RD is tied high and /CS low at the chip, so the bus only ever writes." (at 25.4 25.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid a09c9d54-6f80-57fd-b51d-995f58cf3e62)
  )
  (text "Boot-time pulls: until the firmware starts, these hold the\nYM2612 in reset and keep /WR idle. 4.7k pull-downs: RP2350 erratum E9." (at 101.6 205.74 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 8a235e5c-dee6-51e2-a6a6-4f41e5b050b0)
  )
  (text "Test points for the logic analyzer (milestone M1). They connect by name." (at 292.1 86.36 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 581ca9b2-e2a1-5113-928c-b687a412c65b)
  )
)
